  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-4,-2],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-4)$ and $f(-2).$\n\nSince $f(-4)=5$ and $f(-2)=-3,$ we must have \n$k\\in [-3,5].$\n\nAmong the given options, only $k=2$ belongs to the interval $[-3,5].$",
